Sun Walk — data attribution and licensing
=========================================

D-001 resolved 2026-08-28: the owner accepts ODbL for the OpenStreetMap-derived
pedestrian graph (option A). This NOTICE is the canonical statement; the same
notice appears in README.md, START/README.md, and
.claude/reference/sunwalk/02-data-sources.md.


PEDESTRIAN GRAPH — OpenStreetMap-derived
---------------------------------------
The walkable network Sun Walk routes over is substantially derived from
OpenStreetMap geometry and is a Derivative Database under ODbL.

  © OpenStreetMap contributors

  This Sun Walk pedestrian graph database is made available under the Open
  Database License: http://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1.0/. Any rights in
  individual contents of the database are licensed under the Database Contents
  License: http://opendatacommons.org/licenses/dbcl/1.0/

Scope — this applies to every OSM-derived artifact:
  - sources/osm-tempe.*                     raw / clipped extract
  - build/graph.json                        the derivative database
  - build/graph-{hash}.bin and its manifest.json   the shipped runtime form
  - any GeoJSON export of graph edges or nodes

The Sun Walk map UI MUST display "© OpenStreetMap contributors" wherever the
route or the graph overlay is shown (MapLibre attribution control — ticket T-050).

A local copy of the ODbL 1.0 and DbCL 1.0 texts may be added under LICENSES/ and
the URLs above replaced with local paths.


BUILDING DATA — ASU UFRM
-----------------------
Building footprints, names, categories, addresses, gross square footage, and
photos come from ASU University Facility Records Management (UFRM):
https://services5.arcgis.com/aYs2RC3pluEvAuE3/arcgis/rest/services/CampusBuilding/FeatureServer

Internal university data published without an explicit open license — "use
permitted, redistribution unclear" (see START/07-open-decisions.md#D-002).

UFRM-derived attributes are kept in files SEPARATE from the OSM-derived graph
(sources/ufrm-*, build/catalog-{hash}.json) so the two licences do not mix. Do
not merge UFRM attributes into build/graph.json.


BASEMAP
-------
Development uses https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty. Production will
self-host a PMTiles extract (START/07-open-decisions.md#D-004); its own
attribution requirements apply at that point.
